// Book Five, Chapter 13 (session 57). The sixth of October 1887, a week after Michaelmas.
// Opens with no phase (the lead's report on the sleeper's first week), a late waking scene that only runs if the lid was sealed, a short hunger scene that only runs if must_feed(), then one night phase of three actions out of four, a fixed closing every player plays, and a dawn.
// The coven fronts the chapter: the family has nursed the sleeper through his first week, the business lead keeps the firm and the books, the haven takes in a guest who is older than every house in London, and the firm builds and invests for the winter. Rival covens are the heart of it (the Court of Lamps and the judgment of its Warden, the young houses, the Gaslight Club). Reads b5.waking, b5.stair, b5.hand, b5.offer, b5.stay, b5.club, b5.congress, b5.roofs, b5.order, b5.sat, b5.vigil. Names are always checked with in_circle().
// Sets b5.lid, b5.lisle, b5.meeting, b5.vane and b5.first. Uses send(), coven_task(), acquire(), invest(), discover(), meet(), witness(), earn(), has_gift(), member_has_gift(), gift_holder().
// Ends with rest() and => next, which continues into chapter 14.
@chapter b5c13
@title The Convalescent
@book whitechapel-hunt
@version 1

# start
## The sixth of October
$ b5.lid = "gave"
$ b5.lisle = "guest"
$ b5.meeting = "between"
